{"availability":"available","full":"deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM-Ascend","name":"DeepGEMM-Ascend","description":"DeepGEMM-Ascend: clean and efficient matrix multiplication kernel library for Huawei Ascend NPUs","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":474,"forks":33,"created":"2026-09-29T15:49:55Z","updated":"2026-09-30T01:11:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","stars":474,"forks":33}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DeepGEMM Ascend is a port of DeepGEMM to the HUAWEI Ascend platform. It is fully API-compatible with DeepGEMM and supports BF16, FP8, FP4 GEMM, MQA logits, and MegaMoE. On Ascend platforms, users can simply install the package and use the same APIs and development workflow as DeepGEMM on other supported platforms.","DeepGEMM Ascend provides a lightweight abstraction over the Ascend MAD (matrix multiply-add) primitives, hiding much of the complexity associated with fractal layouts, alignment constraints, address calculations, and verbose low-level parameters. This enables GEMM kernels to remain both concise and efficient. DeepGEMM Ascend makes extensive use of Ascend-specific optimization techniques, such as sparse data loading and coroutine-based pipelining, to approach the performance limits of the Ascend hardware. These implementations can also serve as references for extreme performance optimization…","Despite its lightweight codebase, DeepGEMM Ascend can achieve peak hardware performance across a wide range of matrix shapes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM-Ascend/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c75e9101ed2d429573ec727f4cdac15ba9bdc568ff3c1fac85a1dc131d774a53","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:48.547Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"DeepGEMM Ascend is a port of DeepGEMM to the HUAWEI Ascend platform. It is fully API-compatible with DeepGEMM and supports BF16, FP8, FP4 GEMM, MQA logits, and MegaMoE. On Ascend platforms, users can simply install the package and use the same APIs and development workflow as DeepGEMM on other supported platforms.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM-Ascend/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c75e9101ed2d429573ec727f4cdac15ba9bdc568ff3c1fac85a1dc131d774a53","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM-Ascend/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:48.547Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-30T01:11:39Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:40.599Z","latestRelease":null,"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:40.599Z","screenshots":[],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:42.854Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM-Ascend/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:48.548Z","hash":"c75e9101ed2d429573ec727f4cdac15ba9bdc568ff3c1fac85a1dc131d774a53","originalBytes":11569,"storedBytes":11569,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["ascend","deepgemm","gemm","jit","kernel","deep","fp8","fp4","kernels","layout","default","get","mqa","npu","tflops","alignment","bandwidth","bf16","computation","latency","print","zhou","each","hardware","launch","logits","memory","zhean","cache","compiler","contiguous","deepgemm-ascend","deepseek","experts","home","kexing","performance","required","scaling","tokens","used","across","algorithms","chenggang","debug","deterministic","development","factors","first","gemm.set","grouped","huawei","license","megamoe","mhc","package","path","per","prenorm","support","type","when","zhao","achieve","anyi","api","arch","bash","bin","bisheng","bound","build","cann","cao","chen","chenhao","co